      "content": "I see. But it feels like there's a major difference in depth. Secular groups often seem much more transient or interest-based, whereas religious institutions have that deep-rooted, multi-generational moral authority. Wouldn't you agree that secular alternatives struggle to provide the same level of rigorous, long-term moral stability that religion offers?",
