      "content": "The depth of moral authority is a key point of debate; religious institutions benefit from a transcendent source of legitimacy that secular groups often lack. However, modern secular communities are developing highly resilient moral frameworks built around shared progressive values, human rights, and empirical ethics. While the *source* of stability differs—sacred versus human-derived—secular groups are proving adept at creating durable commitments through shared goals and deep social investment.",
